# Deployment Rules

Read: `docs/deployment/vps.md`, `docs/deployment/staging.md`, `docs/deployment/production.md`, `docs/deployment/github-workflow.md`

## After coding tasks (local agent)

1. **App changed** (`app/**`): `gradlew assembleDebug` in `app/`; report `app/app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk`; if `adb devices` shows `device`, `adb install -r` + launch MainActivity.
2. **Backend only** (`backend/**`): restart local Node (port 3000). Do **not** build APK.
3. **Both**: restart server + build APK.
4. **GitHub**: never auto stage/commit/push unless user asks.

## Production truth

- Local APK does **not** update `https://paycheckbd.com/downloads/paycheck.apk`.
- Upload production APK only when user explicitly requests: shared path `/var/www/payment-checker/shared/downloads/paycheck.apk`.
- Backend live deploy (PM2 reload / release symlink) only when user explicitly requests.
- Prefer: feature branch → test → staging (if available) → production → health check.

## Never

- Force-push `main`
- Deploy untested payment-flow changes directly to production without confirmation
- Overwrite VPS `.env` DB credentials with local `.env` blindly
